From 33f6d5149f2cca75771604c878b5331b48676928 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: keyspark <kevin.on.the.rocks@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 08:43:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] DSpark port: MTP-seeded chained rounds from committed
 hidden state
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Commit paths now capture the last committed row's target hidden state (one
hc-row copy).  A chained round re-grounds the MTP chain on that captured row
— the same conditioning the stock probe gets from a plain decode — and
verifies [next greedy token ++ MTP chain ++ ngram continuation] in one
batched pass through the row-commit path.  Rounds replace the plain decode
between speculative cycles, which cost ~74 ms per cycle on GB10.  Chainless
rounds still require a full-length ngram match: without an acceptance signal
a whole-batch miss costs more than the decode it replaces.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
